TEXT -48 -288 Left 3 ;#77 Diode peak detector
TEXT -48 -216 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fn5kHhNRsz0
TEXT -48 -168 Left 2 ;Adding C1 turns the same diode and resistor into a peak detector: C1 charges through the
TEXT -48 -128 Left 2 ;diode near each positive peak, then bleeds off through R1 until the next one.
TEXT 560 96 Left 2 ;R1 and C1 give a 3.3 ms time constant,
TEXT 560 128 Left 2 ;chosen to match the droop on Alan's screen.
TEXT 560 160 Left 2 ;He says he kept the bleeder small on purpose
TEXT 560 192 Left 2 ;so the droop is easy to see.
